  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The status quo of having only the alternative of the pre-programmed whitelist or allowing any URLs is not good. There are plenty of valid services or people's private streaming servers that you might want to use that are not in the whitelist, which in the end causes everyone who wants to be able to see the content to just select \"Allow Untrusted URLs\" permanently causing this security measure of the whitelist to be a non-measure. (In theory you could leave it unchecked most of the time, and then check it only when you need to. But I think the people who do this are a minority)\nIt's very common to see worlds ask you to check this setting first thing you enter them, because of course, if you don't the world won't function properly.\nIt would be much better if players could curate their own local additions to the whitelist for people and services they trust.\nIt would probably make sense for the client to ask the user the first time an untrusted URL is about to be accessed whether to 1) go forward with it once 2) go forward with it and add this URL to the whitelist 3) deny the access",
